Agree with @joshamaju here. It should be explicitly mentioned in the docs that none of the Context helpers won't work when you return a raw Response. Major frameworks that provide a cookie helper (including SvelteKit, Next.js, Astro) set cookies even when a Response is returned so many users have that expectation. IMO, response helpers shouldn't be inside of the Context object if you can't modify that request context under certain conditions. It's just confusing API design. Separating it to a separate res object for example makes the distinction clear:
