What version of Hono are you using?

3.7.2

What runtime/platform is your app running on?

Node

What steps can reproduce the bug?

Sending a response using any context method i.e html, text etc doesn't work the same way when you just return a Response object. Headers don't get set when using Response
const app = new Hono();

app.get('/', ctx => {
  setCookie(ctx, 'cookie', 'value');
  return ctx.text('html')
})
The cookie header gets discarded in the example below, while it works fine in the example above
const app = new Hono();

app.get('/', ctx => {
  setCookie(ctx, 'cookie', 'value');
  return new Response('html', {'Content-Type': 'text/html'})
})

What is the expected behavior?

There should be not difference in behaviour, cookies should get set in both scenarios

What do you see instead?

Cookies get discarded in the other example

